1
00:00:01,168 --> 00:00:02,544
HEY!

2
00:00:02,544 --> 00:00:04,296
HEY. WOW, IT IS
TRUE WHAT THEY SAY:

3
00:00:04,296 --> 00:00:06,214
PREGNANT BELLIES
LOOK LIKE A DRUM.

4
00:00:08,717 --> 00:00:10,051
HA, HA.

5
00:00:10,051 --> 00:00:11,595
NO, IT'S JUST,
I'M SO PREGNANT

6
00:00:11,595 --> 00:00:13,430
THAT MY GUITAR
DOESN'T FIT ANYMORE

7
00:00:13,430 --> 00:00:14,849
SO I THOUGHT,
TILL I'M NOT

8
00:00:14,849 --> 00:00:16,767
I'M JUST GOING TO
PLAY ALL MY SONGS

9
00:00:16,767 --> 00:00:17,768
ON THIS DRUM.

10
00:00:17,768 --> 00:00:19,353
IT SOUNDS REALLY COOL.

11
00:00:19,353 --> 00:00:20,354
OH, YEAH?

12
00:00:20,354 --> 00:00:21,605
LISTEN, LISTEN.

13
00:00:21,605 --> 00:00:22,564
OKAY.

14
00:00:23,816 --> 00:00:27,194
♪ SMELLY CAT, SMELLY CAT ♪

15
00:00:27,194 --> 00:00:30,364
♪ WHAT ARE THEY FEEDING YOU? ♪

16
00:00:35,202 --> 00:00:36,370
( giggles )

17
00:00:36,370 --> 00:00:38,163
WOW, PHEEBS,
THAT SOUNDS GREAT.

18
00:00:38,163 --> 00:00:40,499
I KNOW, I KNOW! AND
I'VE ONLY BEEN PLAYING

19
00:00:40,499 --> 00:00:41,709
FOR, LIKE, AN HOUR.

20
00:00:41,709 --> 00:00:43,502
HUH.

21
00:00:43,502 --> 00:00:45,587
PHOEBE. PHOEBE, HI.

22
00:00:45,587 --> 00:00:46,714
HI.
HI.
HEY.

23
00:00:46,714 --> 00:00:48,007
WHAT ARE YOU
DOING HERE?

24
00:00:48,007 --> 00:00:49,132
ACTUALLY,
I CAME DOWN

25
00:00:49,132 --> 00:00:50,592
TO ASK YOU
A BIG FAVOR.

26
00:00:50,592 --> 00:00:52,051
OH. WELL, DON'T TELL ME

27
00:00:52,051 --> 00:00:53,136
YOU WANT TO KEEP
MORE OF YOUR STUFF

28
00:00:53,136 --> 00:00:54,638
IN MY UTERUS.

29
00:00:54,638 --> 00:00:56,598
( laughs )

30
00:00:56,598 --> 00:00:57,599
NO, NO, NO.

31
00:00:57,599 --> 00:00:58,600
OH.

32
00:00:58,600 --> 00:01:00,435
OKAY, NOW, SEE...

33
00:01:00,435 --> 00:01:02,855
I WANT TO NAME THE
GIRL BABY "LESLIE"

34
00:01:02,855 --> 00:01:04,356
AND, UM, FRANK WANTS

35
00:01:04,356 --> 00:01:06,608
TO NAME ONE OF
THE BOY BABIES...

36
00:01:06,608 --> 00:01:08,569
"FRANK, JR., JR."

37
00:01:10,029 --> 00:01:12,031
WOULDN'T THAT BE
"FRANK THE THIRD"?

38
00:01:12,031 --> 00:01:13,281
DON'T GET ME STARTED.

39
00:01:15,034 --> 00:01:17,995
ANYWAY, UM, SINCE
THERE ARE THREE BABIES

40
00:01:17,995 --> 00:01:21,623
AND, UM, WE BOTH GOT
TO PUT OUR NAMES IN

41
00:01:21,623 --> 00:01:23,250
WE WOULD BE TRULY HONORED

42
00:01:23,250 --> 00:01:25,377
IF YOU WOULD NAME
THE OTHER BOY BABY.

43
00:01:25,377 --> 00:01:27,170
OH, WOW!

44
00:01:27,170 --> 00:01:28,213
THAT'S SO NICE.

45
00:01:28,213 --> 00:01:30,841
OH! OH! "COUGAR."

46
00:01:32,718 --> 00:01:34,219
YOU THINK ABOUT IT.

47
00:01:34,219 --> 00:01:35,596
YEAH.

48
00:01:35,596 --> 00:01:37,056
YEAH.

49
00:01:42,185 --> 00:01:47,190
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

50
00:01:47,190 --> 00:01:49,443
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

51
00:01:49,443 --> 00:01:51,737
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

52
00:01:51,737 --> 00:01:56,742
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

53
00:01:56,742 --> 00:01:59,160
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN YOUR DAY ♪

54
00:01:59,160 --> 00:02:02,247
♪ YOUR WEEK, YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

55
00:02:02,247 --> 00:02:05,834
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

56
00:02:05,834 --> 00:02:08,211
♪ WHEN THE RAIN
STARTS TO POUR ♪

57
00:02:08,211 --> 00:02:10,881
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

58
00:02:10,881 --> 00:02:13,008
♪ LIKE I'VE BEEN THERE BEFORE ♪

59
00:02:13,008 --> 00:02:15,761
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

60
00:02:15,761 --> 00:02:20,724
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

61
00:02:28,398 --> 00:02:30,442
I LEFT A BRA DRYING
ON THE SHOWER ROD.

62
00:02:30,442 --> 00:02:32,235
YOU DON'T THINK YOUR SON
WILL THINK IT'S YOURS

63
00:02:32,235 --> 00:02:34,071
AND BE HORRIBLY
TRAUMATIZED?

64
00:02:34,071 --> 00:02:35,447
HEY, MOMMY CAN
HAVE A WIFE

65
00:02:35,447 --> 00:02:36,657
DADDY CAN HAVE A BRA.

66
00:02:36,657 --> 00:02:38,533
( both chuckle )

67
00:02:38,533 --> 00:02:40,869
OH, IT'S TIME TO GO.
OH, NO, NO, NO.

68
00:02:40,869 --> 00:02:42,830
SEE, THAT-THAT CLOCK'S
A LITTLE FAST.

69
00:02:42,830 --> 00:02:46,083
UH, WE... WE STILL
HAVE 17 MINUTES.

70
00:02:46,083 --> 00:02:50,796
HUH. WHAT CAN WE DO
IN 17 MINUTES... TWICE?

71
00:02:50,796 --> 00:02:52,464
WOW, THAT'S AMBITIOUS.

72
00:02:52,464 --> 00:02:53,841
MMM...

73
00:02:53,841 --> 00:02:55,050
( knock at door )

74
00:02:55,050 --> 00:02:57,176
OKAY, YOU CAN
IGNORE THAT. IT'S...

75
00:02:57,176 --> 00:02:58,512
THAT'S CAROL
WITH YOUR SON.

76
00:02:58,512 --> 00:02:59,805
UH, BELIEVE ME

77
00:02:59,805 --> 00:03:02,099
WHEN HE'S OLDER,
HE'LL UNDERSTAND.

78
00:03:02,099 --> 00:03:03,350
Carol:
ROSS?

79
00:03:03,350 --> 00:03:04,810
I'LL BE RIGHT THERE.

80
00:03:04,810 --> 00:03:05,978
( groans )

81
00:03:09,857 --> 00:03:11,525
HELLO!
HI.

82
00:03:11,525 --> 00:03:13,360
HELLO.
HELLO.

83
00:03:13,360 --> 00:03:14,402
HI.
HEY.

84
00:03:14,402 --> 00:03:16,071
EMILY, THIS IS
CAROL AND SUSAN.

85
00:03:16,071 --> 00:03:17,781
IT'S SO NICE
TO FINALLY MEET YOU.

86
00:03:17,781 --> 00:03:18,866
YOU, TOO.

87
00:03:18,866 --> 00:03:20,492
SUSAN'S SHOOTING
A COMMERCIAL

88
00:03:20,492 --> 00:03:21,618
IN LONDON NEXT WEEK.

89
00:03:21,618 --> 00:03:22,870
YEAH. I'M SO EXCITED.

90
00:03:22,870 --> 00:03:24,121
I'VE NEVER BEEN THERE.

91
00:03:24,121 --> 00:03:25,122
I'LL SHOW YOU AROUND.

92
00:03:25,122 --> 00:03:26,247
THAT'D BE GREAT.

93
00:03:26,247 --> 00:03:28,000
ALSO, I WAS HOPING
TO CATCH A SHOW.

94
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:30,085
SO, IF YOU CAN MAKE
ANY SUGGESTIONS...

95
00:03:30,085 --> 00:03:31,795
THERE'S TONS OF
TERRIFIC STUFF.

96
00:03:31,795 --> 00:03:33,047
I'LL GO WITH YOU.

97
00:03:33,047 --> 00:03:34,048
AH.

98
00:03:34,048 --> 00:03:35,049
OH, I'M SORRY.

99
00:03:35,049 --> 00:03:36,341
OH, WOW.

100
00:03:36,341 --> 00:03:38,385
OH, LOOK AT YOU TWO,
BONDING

101
00:03:38,385 --> 00:03:40,470
MAKING US LATE
FOR THE AIRPORT, SO...

102
00:03:40,470 --> 00:03:42,347
ARE YOU ALL RIGHT?

103
00:03:42,347 --> 00:03:43,473
HE'S FINE.
HE'S FINE.

104
00:03:43,473 --> 00:03:44,850
IT'S JUST
US GETTING ALONG

105
00:03:44,850 --> 00:03:45,893
IS DIFFICULT
FOR HIM

106
00:03:45,893 --> 00:03:47,186
BECAUSE HE
DOESN'T LIKE ME.

107
00:03:47,186 --> 00:03:48,812
WHAT... OH...

108
00:03:48,812 --> 00:03:51,899
COME ON, THAT'S, THAT'S...
IT'S TRUE.

109
00:03:57,237 --> 00:03:58,780
HI.
Joey:
HEY.

110
00:03:58,780 --> 00:04:00,574
HEY, DO WE HAVE
A BABY NAME YET?

111
00:04:00,574 --> 00:04:02,534
OH, NO. IT'S SO HARD.

112
00:04:02,534 --> 00:04:05,244
I WENT THROUGH THIS WHOLE BOOK
AND FOUND NOTHING.

113
00:04:05,244 --> 00:04:07,664
I WANT A NAME THAT'S REALLY,
LIKE, YOU KNOW

114
00:04:07,664 --> 00:04:10,918
STRONG AND CONFIDENT, YOU KNOW,
LIKE-LIKE "EXXON."

115
00:04:12,878 --> 00:04:14,254
WELL, IT
CERTAINLY WORKED

116
00:04:14,254 --> 00:04:16,255
FOR THAT VALDEZ KID.

117
00:04:16,255 --> 00:04:18,466
OH, OH! PHEEBS,
YOU WANT A STRONG NAME?

118
00:04:18,466 --> 00:04:20,928
HOW ABOUT "THE HULK"?

119
00:04:20,928 --> 00:04:22,054
I DON'T KNOW.

120
00:04:22,054 --> 00:04:23,638
I'M-I'M NOT SURE ABOUT "HULK"

121
00:04:23,638 --> 00:04:26,767
BUT I LIKE THE IDEA
OF A NAME STARTING WITH "THE."

122
00:04:26,767 --> 00:04:28,977
OH, YOU WANT
A GOOD NAME?

123
00:04:28,977 --> 00:04:30,270
GO WITH "JOEY."

124
00:04:30,270 --> 00:04:31,312
JOEY IS YOUR PAL.
JOEY IS YOUR BUDDY.

125
00:04:31,312 --> 00:04:32,606
"WHERE IS EVERYBODY?"

126
00:04:32,606 --> 00:04:36,651
"WELL, THEY'RE HANGING
OUT WITH JOEY."

127
00:04:36,651 --> 00:04:38,028
IF YOU'RE GOING TO DO THAT

128
00:04:38,028 --> 00:04:39,071
IF YOU'RE GOING
TO NAME HIM "JOEY"

129
00:04:39,071 --> 00:04:41,322
YOU SHOULD NAME HIM "CHANDLER."

130
00:04:41,322 --> 00:04:42,991
OH, COME ON--
CHANDLER'S FUNNY

131
00:04:42,991 --> 00:04:45,284
HE'S SOPHISTICATED,
AND HE'S VERY LOVABLE

132
00:04:45,284 --> 00:04:47,121
ONCE YOU GET
TO KNOW HIM.

133
00:04:47,121 --> 00:04:48,122
OH, WELL, HEY

134
00:04:48,122 --> 00:04:49,873
JOEY'S LOVABLE, TOO

135
00:04:49,873 --> 00:04:51,374
BUT THE THING
ABOUT JOEY IS

136
00:04:51,374 --> 00:04:53,710
IF YOU NEED HIM,
HE'LL BE THERE.

137
00:04:53,710 --> 00:04:55,670
WELL, CHANDLER WILL BE
THERE FOR YOU, TOO.

138
00:04:55,670 --> 00:04:58,257
I MEAN, HE MIGHT BE
A LITTLE LATE, BUT...

139
00:04:58,257 --> 00:04:59,466
BUT HE'LL BE THERE

140
00:04:59,466 --> 00:05:01,260
AND HE'LL BRING YOU
SOME COLD SODA

141
00:05:01,260 --> 00:05:04,596
IF WHAT YOU NEED HIM FOR
IS THAT YOU'RE REALLY HOT.

142
00:05:04,596 --> 00:05:05,973
HEY, WHAT
DO YOU SAY?

143
00:05:05,973 --> 00:05:07,141
WHAT DO YOU SAY?

144
00:05:07,141 --> 00:05:09,559
WELL, I...
I LIKE THE IDEA

145
00:05:09,559 --> 00:05:12,020
OF NAMING HIM
AFTER SOMEONE I LOVE

146
00:05:12,020 --> 00:05:15,149
AND "JOEY" AND "CHANDLER"
ARE BOTH GREAT NAMES...

147
00:05:19,486 --> 00:05:22,447
BUT...
ALL RIGHT, I DON'T...

148
00:05:22,447 --> 00:05:26,118
MAYBE I WILL JUST NAME HIM
"THE HULK."

149
00:05:26,118 --> 00:05:27,702
I KNEW I SHOULDN'T
HAVE MENTIONED IT.

150
00:05:27,702 --> 00:05:29,663
THAT'S WHAT I WANTED
TO NAME MY KID.

151
00:05:33,332 --> 00:05:35,252
Rachel:
IF YOU WERE HOPING
TO SLEEP WITH JOSHUA

152
00:05:35,252 --> 00:05:36,753
FOR THE FIRST TIME TONIGHT

153
00:05:36,753 --> 00:05:38,880
WHICH ONE OF THESE
WOULD YOU WANT TO BE WEARING?

154
00:05:38,880 --> 00:05:41,008
YOU KNOW WHAT?
IT REALLY CREEPS ME OUT

155
00:05:41,008 --> 00:05:43,010
CHOOSING OTHER PEOPLE'S
SEX CLOTHES.

156
00:05:43,010 --> 00:05:44,719
OH. I'M SORRY.

157
00:05:44,719 --> 00:05:46,180
I'M JUST SO EXCITED.

158
00:05:46,180 --> 00:05:48,347
I'VE BEEN WAITING FOR THIS FOR
MONTHS.

159
00:05:48,347 --> 00:05:49,641
GOT MY HAIR COLORED.

160
00:05:49,641 --> 00:05:50,809
GOT NEW SHEETS.

161
00:05:50,809 --> 00:05:52,393
MAKING HIM
A VERY FANCY MEAL.

162
00:05:52,393 --> 00:05:53,478
MM-HMM...

163
00:05:53,478 --> 00:05:55,314
WHAT AM I MAKING
HIM, BY THE WAY?

164
00:05:55,314 --> 00:05:57,858
WELL, YOU'RE MAKING
HIM A FRISEE SALAD

165
00:05:57,858 --> 00:06:00,027
WITH GOAT CHEESE
AND PINE NUTS

166
00:06:00,027 --> 00:06:02,321
WILD RICE,
ROASTED ASPARAGUS

167
00:06:02,321 --> 00:06:04,156
AND SALMON EN CROUTE.

168
00:06:04,156 --> 00:06:07,742
I THOUGHT I WAS
MAKING HIM FILET MIGNON.

169
00:06:07,742 --> 00:06:09,328
YEAH, YOU WERE, BUT THEN
YOU DECIDED TO MAKE SALMON

170
00:06:09,328 --> 00:06:11,955
BECAUSE YOU HAD SOME
LEFTOVER AT THE RESTAURANT

171
00:06:11,955 --> 00:06:13,623
AND THEN YOU REALIZED IF
YOU BITCHED ABOUT IT

172
00:06:13,623 --> 00:06:15,458
THEN YOU WOULD
STOP COOKING

173
00:06:15,458 --> 00:06:17,376
AND YOU WOULD HAVE TO MAKE
YOUR FAMOUS BAKED POTATO

174
00:06:17,376 --> 00:06:20,005
AND DIET COKE.

175
00:06:20,005 --> 00:06:22,049
WOW, I REALLY GET CRABBY
WHEN I COOK.

176
00:06:22,049 --> 00:06:23,342
( mirthless chuckle )

177
00:06:25,010 --> 00:06:26,011
HEY.

178
00:06:26,011 --> 00:06:28,013
All:
HEY.

179
00:06:28,013 --> 00:06:30,389
SO, UH, EMILY
CALLED LAST NIGHT.

180
00:06:30,389 --> 00:06:33,935
AND NOW YOU'RE
GIVING ME THE MESSAGE?

181
00:06:36,688 --> 00:06:41,235
TURNS OUT THAT EMILY
IS JUST CRAZY ABOUT SUSAN. YEAH.

182
00:06:41,235 --> 00:06:44,238
THEY'RE GOING
TO THE THEATER TOGETHER...

183
00:06:44,238 --> 00:06:46,823
THEY'RE GOING TO DINNER...

184
00:06:46,823 --> 00:06:49,117
THEY'RE GOING HORSEBACK RIDING.

185
00:06:49,117 --> 00:06:51,995
GOD, SUSAN IS SO FUN.

186
00:06:51,995 --> 00:06:54,081
( chuckles )

187
00:06:55,582 --> 00:06:59,086
LOOK, THIS IS JUST A LITTLE
TOO FAMILIAR, OKAY?

188
00:06:59,086 --> 00:07:02,130
FOR-FOR LIKE SIX MONTHS
BEFORE CAROL AND I SPLIT UP

189
00:07:02,130 --> 00:07:06,425
ALL I HEARD WAS, "MY FRIEND
SUSAN IS-IS SO SMART."

190
00:07:06,425 --> 00:07:08,469
"MY FRIEND SUSAN IS SO FUNNY."

191
00:07:08,469 --> 00:07:10,805
"MY FRIEND SUSAN IS SO GREAT."

192
00:07:10,805 --> 00:07:12,224
YOU ACTUALLY THINK

193
00:07:12,224 --> 00:07:13,516
THAT SOMETHING
COULD HAPPEN

194
00:07:13,516 --> 00:07:15,018
BETWEEN EMILY
AND SUSAN?

195
00:07:15,018 --> 00:07:18,313
HEY, THEY'RE GOING
TO THE GYM TOGETHER.

196
00:07:19,398 --> 00:07:21,191
TWO WOMEN?

197
00:07:21,191 --> 00:07:22,234
STRETCHING?

198
00:07:22,234 --> 00:07:24,111
YOU KNOW, THEY TAKE

199
00:07:24,111 --> 00:07:26,863
A STEAM TOGETHER,
THINGS GET A LITTLE PLAYFUL...

200
00:07:26,863 --> 00:07:28,531
DIDN'T YOU SEE PERSONAL BEST?

201
00:07:28,531 --> 00:07:29,866
NO, BUT I'M GONNA.

202
00:07:32,744 --> 00:07:35,247
HI! HI! YOU'RE CRAZY.

203
00:07:35,247 --> 00:07:36,248
THIS IS EMILY.

204
00:07:36,248 --> 00:07:37,874
EMILY IS STRAIGHT.

205
00:07:37,874 --> 00:07:39,209
YEAH, HOW
DO YOU KNOW?

206
00:07:39,209 --> 00:07:40,627
I MEAN, WE THOUGHT
CAROL WAS STRAIGHT

207
00:07:40,627 --> 00:07:42,670
BEFORE I
MARRIED HER.

208
00:07:42,670 --> 00:07:44,047
YEAH, I'M DEFINITELY...

209
00:07:44,047 --> 00:07:46,133
I DON'T LIKE
THE NAME "ROSS."

210
00:07:49,136 --> 00:07:51,972
WHAT A WEIRD WAY TO
KICK ME WHEN I'M DOWN.

211
00:07:51,972 --> 00:07:55,142
NO, NO. NO, I JUST...
I MEANT FOR THE BABY.

212
00:07:55,142 --> 00:07:58,103
OH.

213
00:07:58,103 --> 00:08:00,647
WHAT'S WRONG
WITH "ROSS"?

214
00:08:00,647 --> 00:08:03,024
WELL, IT'S JUST, YOU KNOW
SOMETHING LIKE THIS
WOULD NEVER HAPPEN

215
00:08:03,024 --> 00:08:04,776
TO, LIKE,
THE HULK, YOU KNOW.

216
00:08:06,569 --> 00:08:08,529
ACTUALLY, THAT-
THAT'S NOT TRUE.

217
00:08:08,529 --> 00:08:10,949
IN THE INCREDIBLE
HULK, UH, NUMBER 72

218
00:08:10,949 --> 00:08:12,826
DR. BRUCE BANNER
FOUND-FOUND...

219
00:08:14,911 --> 00:08:16,496
YOU KNOW... NEVER MIND.

220
00:08:16,496 --> 00:08:18,957
MY GIRLFRIEND'S
A LESBIAN.

221
00:08:18,957 --> 00:08:20,834
SO, I DECIDED

222
00:08:20,834 --> 00:08:22,669
I'M DEFINITELY GOING TO GO

223
00:08:22,669 --> 00:08:24,503
WITH EITHER "JOEY"
OR "CHANDLER."

224
00:08:24,503 --> 00:08:25,505
OH!

225
00:08:25,505 --> 00:08:26,506
OH, OH, OH, OH!

226
00:08:26,506 --> 00:08:28,133
YOU GOT TO PICK "JOEY."

227
00:08:28,133 --> 00:08:30,927
I MEAN, NAME ONE FAMOUS
PERSON NAMED "CHANDLER."

228
00:08:30,927 --> 00:08:32,387
RAYMOND CHANDLER.

229
00:08:32,387 --> 00:08:33,888
SOMEONE YOU DIDN'T MAKE UP.

230
00:08:33,888 --> 00:08:35,556
( scoffs )

231
00:08:35,556 --> 00:08:38,101
OKAY, THERE ARE NO
FAMOUS "JOEYS," EXCEPT FOR...

232
00:08:38,101 --> 00:08:39,102
( chuckles )

233
00:08:39,102 --> 00:08:40,603
JOEY BUTTAFUOCO.

234
00:08:40,603 --> 00:08:43,857
YEAH, THAT GUY REALLY HURT US.

235
00:08:43,857 --> 00:08:45,566
YEAH.

236
00:08:45,566 --> 00:08:47,777
WELL, HOW ABOUT A COMPROMISE,
THEN, OKAY?

237
00:08:47,777 --> 00:08:49,904
WHAT IF IT'S, YOU KNOW...
"CHANOEY"?

238
00:08:49,904 --> 00:08:51,198
OKAY, LOOK--
"JOEY"?

239
00:08:51,198 --> 00:08:52,615
COME ON, THINK ABOUT IT.

240
00:08:52,615 --> 00:08:54,742
FIRST OF ALL,
HE'LL NEVER BE PRESIDENT.

241
00:08:54,742 --> 00:08:57,954
I MEAN, THERE'S NEVER GOING
TO BE A PRESIDENT JOEY.

242
00:08:57,954 --> 00:09:00,374
ALL RIGHT, MAN,
I DIDN'T WANT TO BRING THIS UP

243
00:09:00,374 --> 00:09:02,376
BUT "CHANDLER"
IS THE STUPIDEST NAME

244
00:09:02,376 --> 00:09:03,751
I EVER HEARD IN MY LIFE.

245
00:09:03,751 --> 00:09:05,879
IT'S NOT EVEN A NAME.

246
00:09:05,879 --> 00:09:07,588
IT'S BARELY EVEN A WORD, OKAY?

247
00:09:07,588 --> 00:09:11,510
IT'S KIND OF LIKE "CHANDELIER"
BUT IT'S NOT.

248
00:09:11,510 --> 00:09:12,760
ALL RIGHT?

249
00:09:12,760 --> 00:09:15,722
IT'S A STUPID, STUPID NON-NAME.

250
00:09:19,893 --> 00:09:22,396
WOW, YOU... YOU'RE RIGHT.

251
00:09:22,396 --> 00:09:25,899
I HAVE
A HORRIBLE, HORRIBLE NAME.

252
00:09:27,484 --> 00:09:28,818
( sighs )

253
00:09:28,818 --> 00:09:30,320
I'M SORRY, MAN.
I DIDN'T...

254
00:09:30,320 --> 00:09:31,530
I'M-I'M SORRY.
I'M SORRY.

255
00:09:31,530 --> 00:09:32,864
OKAY.

256
00:09:32,864 --> 00:09:35,574
SO, I GUESS IT'S
"JOEY," THEN.

257
00:09:43,624 --> 00:09:44,959
THIS IS SO NICE.

258
00:09:44,959 --> 00:09:46,503
THANK YOU
FOR DOING THIS.

259
00:09:46,503 --> 00:09:49,797
OH, PLEASE. COOKING SOOTHES ME.

260
00:09:49,797 --> 00:09:51,466
( both chuckle )

261
00:09:53,176 --> 00:09:55,429
( sighs )
SO, DIG IN.

262
00:09:55,429 --> 00:09:58,473
RIGHT. OH, IT ALL
LOOKS SO GOOD.

263
00:09:58,473 --> 00:09:59,558
MMM.

264
00:09:59,558 --> 00:10:00,850
MMM!

265
00:10:02,477 --> 00:10:03,811
OH, MY GOD.

266
00:10:03,811 --> 00:10:04,854
OH, I KNOW.

267
00:10:04,854 --> 00:10:06,273
MY GOD, THIS IS SO...

268
00:10:06,273 --> 00:10:07,482
THIS RICE IS SO...

269
00:10:07,482 --> 00:10:08,775
I'M SO GOOD.

270
00:10:08,775 --> 00:10:09,776
BEHIND YOU.

271
00:10:10,860 --> 00:10:12,571
OH, YEAH, SORRY.

272
00:10:12,571 --> 00:10:13,863
THEY USED TO LIVE HERE

273
00:10:13,863 --> 00:10:15,990
AND SOMETIMES
THEY MIGRATE BACK OVER.

274
00:10:15,990 --> 00:10:18,368
IS THERE, UH...
IS THERE SOME WAY

275
00:10:18,368 --> 00:10:20,620
THAT THEY COULD, UH...
NOT BE HERE?

276
00:10:20,620 --> 00:10:23,957
IT'S JUST THAT, UH, FARM BIRDS
REALLY KIND OF FREAK ME OUT.

277
00:10:23,957 --> 00:10:25,917
YEAH, SURE, OKAY. OKAY.

278
00:10:25,917 --> 00:10:26,918
OKAY, GREAT.

279
00:10:26,918 --> 00:10:28,128
COME ON.
SHOO. SHOO.

280
00:10:28,128 --> 00:10:29,670
HERE WE GO.
HERE WE GO. WHOA!

281
00:10:29,670 --> 00:10:30,880
SHOO. SHOO.

282
00:10:30,880 --> 00:10:32,591
ALL RIGHT. WHOA!

283
00:10:32,591 --> 00:10:33,716
OH, SORRY.
COME HERE.

284
00:10:33,716 --> 00:10:34,842
GOOD. THERE YOU GO.

285
00:10:34,842 --> 00:10:36,136
OKAY.

286
00:10:38,221 --> 00:10:39,847
( Joshua clears throat )

287
00:10:44,852 --> 00:10:47,439
HEY, HOW'D YOU DO THAT?

288
00:10:47,439 --> 00:10:49,441
COME ON.

289
00:10:49,441 --> 00:10:50,650
COME HERE.

290
00:10:50,650 --> 00:10:51,651
ALL GONE.

291
00:10:51,651 --> 00:10:52,651
( weak chuckle )

292
00:10:52,651 --> 00:10:54,404
SO, FARM BIRDS, HUH?

293
00:10:54,404 --> 00:10:57,115
YEAH. IT'S, UH, IT'S
MY ONLY WEIRD THING, I SWEAR.

294
00:10:57,115 --> 00:10:59,117
AND I-I-I WOULD'VE TOLD YOU
ABOUT IT

295
00:10:59,117 --> 00:11:01,744
BUT I DIDN'T KNOW
THAT THEY WOULD... BE HERE.

296
00:11:01,744 --> 00:11:03,497
( chuckles ):
OH, OKAY.

297
00:11:03,497 --> 00:11:04,498
SO, ALL RIGHT...

298
00:11:04,498 --> 00:11:06,374
( clears throat )

299
00:11:06,374 --> 00:11:07,542
( chuckles )

300
00:11:07,542 --> 00:11:09,210
OKAY.
( nervous groan )

301
00:11:09,210 --> 00:11:11,754
SO, CAN I SERVE YOU
A LITTLE OF...

302
00:11:11,754 --> 00:11:13,006
WHAT? WHAT'S...? WHAT?

303
00:11:13,006 --> 00:11:14,882
NOTHING. I, UH...

304
00:11:14,882 --> 00:11:19,429
IT'S JUST THAT I KNOW THAT
THEY'RE STILL OUT THERE.

305
00:11:19,429 --> 00:11:21,055
BUT THEY'RE ACROSS THE HALL.

306
00:11:21,055 --> 00:11:22,849
I MEAN, THAT'S TWO DOORS AWAY.

307
00:11:22,849 --> 00:11:24,767
IT'S GOING TO TAKE THEM
A LONG TIME

308
00:11:24,767 --> 00:11:26,853
TO PECK THEIR WAY
BACK OVER HERE.

309
00:11:26,853 --> 00:11:28,229
( nervous chuckle )

310
00:11:28,229 --> 00:11:31,065
HEY, THAT'S-THAT'S
NOT FUNNY.

311
00:11:31,065 --> 00:11:32,233
UH...

312
00:11:32,233 --> 00:11:33,901
OKAY, YOU KNOW...

313
00:11:33,901 --> 00:11:35,069
WOULD YOU FEEL BETTER

314
00:11:35,069 --> 00:11:36,571
IF WE WENT
SOMEPLACE ELSE?

315
00:11:36,571 --> 00:11:38,739
I MEAN, WE COULD PACK
ALL THIS STUFF UP

316
00:11:38,739 --> 00:11:40,741
AND, YOU KNOW,
GO TO YOUR APARTMENT.

317
00:11:40,741 --> 00:11:42,369
OH, THEY'RE WORKING
ON IT THIS WEEK.

318
00:11:42,369 --> 00:11:43,911
IT'S A TOTAL MESS.

319
00:11:43,911 --> 00:11:45,746
BUT I'M STAYING AT
MY PARENTS' HOUSE.

320
00:11:45,746 --> 00:11:46,998
WE COULD GO THERE.

321
00:11:46,998 --> 00:11:48,791
YOUR PARENTS?
THEY'RE OUT OF TOWN.

322
00:11:48,791 --> 00:11:50,669
OH.

323
00:11:50,669 --> 00:11:53,213
YEAH, IT'S A HUGE PLACE,
AND-AND IT'S GOT

324
00:11:53,213 --> 00:11:54,922
THIS GORGEOUS VIEW
OF THE PARK.

325
00:11:54,922 --> 00:11:56,424
IT'D BE VERY,
VERY ROMANTIC.

326
00:11:56,424 --> 00:11:58,009
WHAT DO YOU SAY?

327
00:11:58,009 --> 00:12:00,470
YEAH, THAT WORKS.

328
00:12:00,470 --> 00:12:02,138
( clucking )

329
00:12:02,138 --> 00:12:04,098
YEAH, THEY-THEY CAN
SMELL THE FEAR.

330
00:12:04,098 --> 00:12:05,559
OKAY, IT'S OKAY.

331
00:12:05,559 --> 00:12:06,893
( clears throat )

332
00:12:06,893 --> 00:12:08,395
HEY.
HI.

333
00:12:08,395 --> 00:12:09,604
HOW'S BEN?

334
00:12:09,604 --> 00:12:11,981
WELL, I ASKED HIM
IF HE WANTED TO EAT

335
00:12:11,981 --> 00:12:13,107
HE SAID, "NO."

336
00:12:13,107 --> 00:12:14,859
I ASKED HIM
IF HE WANTED TO SLEEP

337
00:12:14,859 --> 00:12:15,943
HE SAID, "NO."

338
00:12:15,943 --> 00:12:17,612
I ASKED HIM
WHAT HE WANTED TO DO

339
00:12:17,612 --> 00:12:20,865
HE SAID, "NO,"
SO HE'S SWEEPING.

340
00:12:20,865 --> 00:12:22,909
HEY, BUDDY.

341
00:12:22,909 --> 00:12:23,951
HEY.

342
00:12:23,951 --> 00:12:24,952
SO, UM...

343
00:12:24,952 --> 00:12:27,163
ANY WORD FROM SUSAN?

344
00:12:27,163 --> 00:12:28,747
OH, YEAH. SHE SAID

345
00:12:28,747 --> 00:12:30,875
SHE'S HAVING SO MUCH FUN
WITH EMILY.

346
00:12:30,875 --> 00:12:32,877
UH-HUH, UH-HUH.

347
00:12:32,877 --> 00:12:36,089
UH, BY THE BY, DID IT, UH...

348
00:12:36,089 --> 00:12:38,925
DID IT EVER OCCUR TO YOU
THAT, I DON'T KNOW

349
00:12:38,925 --> 00:12:42,011
MAYBE THEY MIGHT BE HAVING
A LITTLE TOO MUCH FUN?

350
00:12:42,011 --> 00:12:43,722
WHAT'S "TOO MUCH FUN"?

351
00:12:43,722 --> 00:12:46,140
YOU KNOW, THE KIND OF FUN
YOU AND SUSAN HAD

352
00:12:46,140 --> 00:12:47,392
WHEN WE WERE MARRIED.

353
00:12:47,392 --> 00:12:48,393
( chuckles )

354
00:12:48,393 --> 00:12:50,811
OH, MY GOD, YOU ARE SO PARANOID.

355
00:12:50,811 --> 00:12:52,606
AM I?
YES.

356
00:12:52,606 --> 00:12:54,315
AM I?

357
00:12:54,315 --> 00:12:55,983
LOOK, I CAN'T
SPEAK FOR EMILY

358
00:12:55,983 --> 00:12:58,777
BUT SUSAN IS IN A LOVING,
COMMITTED RELATIONSHIP.

359
00:12:58,777 --> 00:13:01,656
UH-HUH, CAROL,
SO WERE WE.

360
00:13:01,656 --> 00:13:04,825
ALL RIGHT, JUST IMAGINE
FOR A MOMENT

361
00:13:04,825 --> 00:13:08,496
THAT SUSAN MEETS SOMEONE,
AND THEY REALLY HIT IT OFF.

362
00:13:08,496 --> 00:13:10,789
SAY THEY'RE COMING BACK
FROM THE THEATER

363
00:13:10,789 --> 00:13:13,501
AND THEY STOP AT A PUB
FOR A COUPLE OF DRINKS.

364
00:13:13,501 --> 00:13:15,962
THEY'RE LAUGHING,
YOU KNOW.

365
00:13:15,962 --> 00:13:18,506
SOMEONE INNOCENTLY
TOUCHES SOMEONE ELSE.

366
00:13:18,506 --> 00:13:20,841
THERE'S ELECTRICITY.

367
00:13:20,841 --> 00:13:22,761
IT'S NEW, IT'S EXCITING.

368
00:13:22,761 --> 00:13:24,137
ARE YOU TELLING ME

369
00:13:24,137 --> 00:13:26,723
THERE ISN'T EVEN
THE SLIGHTEST POSSIBILITY

370
00:13:26,723 --> 00:13:29,350
OF SOMETHING HAPPENING?

371
00:13:29,350 --> 00:13:30,602
MAYBE...

372
00:13:30,602 --> 00:13:32,061
OH MY GOD!

373
00:13:32,061 --> 00:13:34,355
I DIDN'T REALLY BELIEVE IT
UNTIL YOU SAID IT!

374
00:13:38,859 --> 00:13:41,279
...AND EVEN THOUGH
NONE OF THE KIDS BELIEVED ME

375
00:13:41,279 --> 00:13:43,531
I SWEAR TO GOD,
THAT DUCK PUSHED ME.

376
00:13:43,531 --> 00:13:44,783
YEAH.

377
00:13:44,783 --> 00:13:47,826
WOW, THIS PLACE
IS FABULOUS!

378
00:13:47,826 --> 00:13:49,287
LET ME SHOW YOU AROUND.

379
00:13:49,287 --> 00:13:51,205
THIS IS THE DOWNSTAIRS
LIVING ROOM...

380
00:13:51,205 --> 00:13:53,082
WHAT? THERE'S TWO LIVING ROOMS?

381
00:13:53,082 --> 00:13:54,584
GOD, GROWING UP HERE

382
00:13:54,584 --> 00:13:57,170
THIS PLACE MUST
HAVE BEEN A REAL BABE MAGNET.

383
00:13:57,170 --> 00:13:59,380
YEAH, WELL,
IT WOULD HAVE BEEN

384
00:13:59,380 --> 00:14:01,675
BUT MY PARENTS
JUST MOVED HERE.

385
00:14:01,675 --> 00:14:03,050
OH, WELL, YOU
SHOULD KNOW

386
00:14:03,050 --> 00:14:04,636
THIS PLACE IS
A REAL BABE MAGNET.

387
00:14:04,636 --> 00:14:06,220
WANT TO MAKE OUT?

388
00:14:06,220 --> 00:14:07,764
YEAH. OKAY.

389
00:14:07,764 --> 00:14:09,140
MMM.

390
00:14:09,140 --> 00:14:10,475
HERE'S AN IDEA.

391
00:14:10,475 --> 00:14:13,478
WHY DON'T I PUT THE FOOD
IN THE FRIDGE

392
00:14:13,478 --> 00:14:16,189
AND WE CAN EAT IT LATER?

393
00:14:16,189 --> 00:14:18,358
THAT SOUNDS LIKE A PLAN.

394
00:14:18,358 --> 00:14:21,486
UM, IS THERE A PLACE THAT
I COULD GO FRESHEN UP?

395
00:14:21,486 --> 00:14:22,487
YEAH, YEAH.

396
00:14:22,487 --> 00:14:23,863
UM, JUST DOWN THE HALL

397
00:14:23,863 --> 00:14:25,990
AND, UH, SECOND DOOR
TO YOUR LEFT.

398
00:14:28,242 --> 00:14:29,910
OH, HI, DARLING.

399
00:14:29,910 --> 00:14:32,246
MOM, DAD! WHAT ARE
YOU GUYS DOING HERE?

400
00:14:32,246 --> 00:14:33,832
WE CUT THE TRIP SHORT.

401
00:14:33,832 --> 00:14:36,376
FRANCE SUCKS!

402
00:14:36,376 --> 00:14:39,212
UM, THIS MAY BE A LITTLE WEIRD

403
00:14:39,212 --> 00:14:41,214
BUT I... I'VE GOT A DATE HERE.

404
00:14:41,214 --> 00:14:42,674
WELL, SAY NO MORE.

405
00:14:42,674 --> 00:14:44,718
WE'LL GRAB SOME FOOD
AND TAKE IT UPSTAIRS

406
00:14:44,718 --> 00:14:46,010
AND BE OUT OF YOUR HAIR.

407
00:14:46,010 --> 00:14:47,220
OH, THAT'D BE GREAT.

408
00:14:47,220 --> 00:14:48,971
SO, YOU DIDN'T GET TO ITALY?

409
00:14:48,971 --> 00:14:50,431
YEP. SUCKS!

410
00:15:14,372 --> 00:15:17,083
HI, YOU.

411
00:15:17,083 --> 00:15:19,794
OH, MY GOD...

412
00:15:19,794 --> 00:15:20,795
I KNOW.

413
00:15:20,795 --> 00:15:22,963
I CAN DO MORE THAN COOK.

414
00:15:24,048 --> 00:15:25,592
UH...

415
00:15:28,969 --> 00:15:30,971
I LIKE HER.

416
00:15:30,971 --> 00:15:33,140
SHE SEEMS SMART.

417
00:15:37,562 --> 00:15:39,021
UH... RACHEL,
MY PARENTS.

418
00:15:39,021 --> 00:15:40,481
OH, SO NICE
TO MEET YOU.

419
00:15:40,481 --> 00:15:41,482
HI, RACHEL.

420
00:15:41,482 --> 00:15:42,942
HELLO. HELLO.

421
00:15:44,318 --> 00:15:46,320
OH, JOSHUA...

422
00:15:46,320 --> 00:15:49,657
THAT $500 WAS
FOR GROCERIES.

423
00:15:51,950 --> 00:15:53,745
WHAT? TH-TH-THIS? NO.
OH, NO, THIS IS NOT...

424
00:15:53,745 --> 00:15:56,163
THAT'S NOT WHAT...
THAT'S NOT WHAT IT IS.

425
00:15:56,163 --> 00:15:58,416
YOU SEE, OKAY,
I WORK IN FASHION.

426
00:15:58,416 --> 00:16:01,461
SEE, AND-AND THIS IS
A REAL DRESS, ACTUALLY.

427
00:16:01,461 --> 00:16:03,003
IT IS...
THEY'RE-THEY'RE

428
00:16:03,003 --> 00:16:04,130
WEARING IT IN MILAN.

429
00:16:04,130 --> 00:16:05,590
IT'S TH... AND...

430
00:16:05,590 --> 00:16:08,259
SEE, OH, PART OF MY JOB
IS TO WEAR THE CLOTHES

431
00:16:08,259 --> 00:16:10,303
AND THEN I SEE
HOW PEOPLE RESPOND

432
00:16:10,303 --> 00:16:11,679
AND THEN I REPORT BACK

433
00:16:11,679 --> 00:16:13,765
TO MY SUPERIORS
AT BLOOMINGDALE'S.

434
00:16:13,765 --> 00:16:15,850
SO...

435
00:16:15,850 --> 00:16:19,103
AND, OBVIOUSLY, IN, UH,
IN-IN THIS CASE

436
00:16:19,103 --> 00:16:21,481
I AM-AM GOING TO REPORT BACK

437
00:16:21,481 --> 00:16:25,359
"U.S.A. NOT READY."

438
00:16:25,359 --> 00:16:26,694
MAYBE IN L.A.

439
00:16:26,694 --> 00:16:27,695
YES.

440
00:16:27,695 --> 00:16:28,863
THERE YOU GO.

441
00:16:28,863 --> 00:16:30,949
SO, HAVE YOU KIDS
EATEN YET?

442
00:16:30,949 --> 00:16:31,950
WELL, WE WERE GOING
TO DO THAT AFTER.

443
00:16:31,950 --> 00:16:34,619
I MEAN, UM...

444
00:16:34,619 --> 00:16:35,870
NEXT.

445
00:16:35,870 --> 00:16:37,079
WELL, WE'RE STARVING.

446
00:16:37,079 --> 00:16:38,706
WHY DON'T WE
GET SOMETHING TO EAT?

447
00:16:38,706 --> 00:16:39,874
OH... YEAH.

448
00:16:39,874 --> 00:16:41,501
WELL...

449
00:16:41,501 --> 00:16:45,964
YEAH, NO USE WASTING THIS BABY
JUST LYING AROUND THE HOUSE.

450
00:16:45,964 --> 00:16:47,882
SO... WE'LL GO EAT.

451
00:16:47,882 --> 00:16:48,967
Rachel:
YEAH.

452
00:16:48,967 --> 00:16:50,802
YOU'LL WEAR THAT.

453
00:16:50,802 --> 00:16:54,305
WE'LL BE EATING, AND, OF COURSE,
YOU'LL BE... WEARING THAT.

454
00:16:56,683 --> 00:16:59,602
DUDE, I AM SORRY
ABOUT WHAT I SAID.

455
00:16:59,602 --> 00:17:01,020
NOPE, NOPE,
YOU'RE RIGHT.

456
00:17:01,020 --> 00:17:03,439
IT IS A RIDICULOUS NAME.

457
00:17:03,439 --> 00:17:04,899
IT'S NOT THAT BAD.

458
00:17:04,899 --> 00:17:07,109
YES, IT IS.

459
00:17:07,109 --> 00:17:10,947
FROM NOW ON, I HAVE
NO FIRST NAME.

460
00:17:10,947 --> 00:17:12,114
SO...

461
00:17:12,114 --> 00:17:13,908
YOU'RE JUST BING?

462
00:17:16,118 --> 00:17:18,538
I HAVE NO NAME.

463
00:17:18,538 --> 00:17:21,248
ALL RIGHT, SO, WHAT ARE WE
SUPPOSED TO CALL YOU?

464
00:17:21,248 --> 00:17:23,668
OKAY, UH, FOR
NOW, TEMPORARILY

465
00:17:23,668 --> 00:17:25,252
YOU CAN CALL ME....

466
00:17:25,252 --> 00:17:26,504
CLINT.

467
00:17:26,504 --> 00:17:28,006
( snickers )

468
00:17:28,006 --> 00:17:30,884
NO WAY ARE YOU COOL ENOUGH
TO PULL OFF CLINT.

469
00:17:30,884 --> 00:17:34,094
OKAY, SO, WHAT NAME AM I
COOL ENOUGH TO PULL OFF?

470
00:17:34,094 --> 00:17:36,014
UM... GENE.

471
00:17:38,933 --> 00:17:42,645
IT'S CLINT.
IT'S CLINT!

472
00:17:42,645 --> 00:17:43,855
SEE YOU LATER, GENE.
BYE, GENE.

473
00:17:45,690 --> 00:17:47,025
IT'S CLINT!

474
00:17:47,025 --> 00:17:48,568
CLINT!

475
00:17:51,362 --> 00:17:53,239
WHAT'S UP WITH GENE?

476
00:17:57,284 --> 00:17:58,828
Monica:
YOU WORE YOUR NIGHTIE
TO DINNER?

477
00:17:58,828 --> 00:18:00,079
OH, YEAH.

478
00:18:00,079 --> 00:18:01,789
AND, UH, THE
BEST PART, THOUGH

479
00:18:01,789 --> 00:18:04,208
WAS WHEN THE, UH, WAITER
SPILLED WATER DOWN MY BACK.

480
00:18:04,208 --> 00:18:06,126
I JUMPED UP AND
MY BOOB POPPED OUT.

481
00:18:06,126 --> 00:18:08,128
OH, MY GOD.
OH, NO.

482
00:18:08,128 --> 00:18:10,048
IT'S ALL RIGHT--
I GOT NICE BOOBS.

483
00:18:13,676 --> 00:18:15,887
SO, I JUST PICKED UP
A MESSAGE FROM EMILY.

484
00:18:15,887 --> 00:18:19,432
SHE AND SUSAN ARE GOING
TO A POETRY READING TOGETHER.

485
00:18:19,432 --> 00:18:20,433
SO?

486
00:18:20,433 --> 00:18:21,726
SO?

487
00:18:21,726 --> 00:18:23,728
POETRY?

488
00:18:23,728 --> 00:18:25,730
SUSAN'S GAY.

489
00:18:25,730 --> 00:18:27,440
THEY'RE BEING GAY TOGETHER!

490
00:18:29,067 --> 00:18:30,610
BUT EMILY'S STRAIGHT.

491
00:18:30,610 --> 00:18:32,361
OH, WAKE UP!

492
00:18:34,405 --> 00:18:35,782
WOW...

493
00:18:35,782 --> 00:18:38,325
CAROL REALLY
MESSED YOU UP.

494
00:18:38,325 --> 00:18:39,911
EXCUSE ME?

495
00:18:39,911 --> 00:18:41,621
YEAH, SHE TURNED YOU
INTO THIS-THIS-THIS

496
00:18:41,621 --> 00:18:46,417
UNTRUSTING, CRAZY,
JEALOUS SYCOPHANT.

497
00:18:48,294 --> 00:18:50,797
ALL RIGHT, SO I DON'T KNOW
WHAT SYCOPHANT MEANS

498
00:18:50,797 --> 00:18:53,758
BUT THE REST IS RIGHT.

499
00:18:53,758 --> 00:18:55,134
I DON'T KNOW
WHAT YOU'RE TALKING ABOUT.

500
00:18:55,134 --> 00:18:57,470
I AM NOT A CRAZY,
JEALOUS PERSON.

501
00:18:57,470 --> 00:18:59,055
HUH.

502
00:18:59,055 --> 00:19:00,932
WHAT?

503
00:19:00,932 --> 00:19:02,516
SHE'S TOTALLY RIGHT.

504
00:19:02,516 --> 00:19:03,768
WHEN WE WERE TOGETHER,

505
00:19:03,768 --> 00:19:05,269
YOU GOT FREAKED OUT ABOUT MARK

506
00:19:05,269 --> 00:19:06,604
AND NOTHING WAS GOING ON.

507
00:19:06,604 --> 00:19:08,106
THIS TOTALLY
MAKES SENSE.

508
00:19:08,106 --> 00:19:09,774
IT DOES NOT.

509
00:19:09,774 --> 00:19:11,400
SURE IT DOES.
IN HIGH SCHOOL

510
00:19:11,400 --> 00:19:12,944
YOU WEREN'T
JEALOUS AT ALL

511
00:19:12,944 --> 00:19:14,862
EVEN THOUGH ALL
YOUR GIRLFRIENDS

512
00:19:14,862 --> 00:19:15,947
WERE CHEATING
ON YOU.

513
00:19:15,947 --> 00:19:17,031
( Phoebe gasps )

514
00:19:17,031 --> 00:19:18,699
ALL RIGHT, ALL RIGHT

515
00:19:18,699 --> 00:19:20,910
SO, UP UNTIL '92, '93,
HE WAS VERY TRUSTING.

516
00:19:20,910 --> 00:19:22,954
THEN '94 HIT,
CAROL LEFT HIM

517
00:19:22,954 --> 00:19:24,622
AND BAM, PARANOID CITY.

518
00:19:24,622 --> 00:19:26,833
Rachel:
YEP. ABSOLUTELY.

519
00:19:26,833 --> 00:19:27,834
ABSOLUTELY.

520
00:19:27,834 --> 00:19:28,876
THIS IS SO MUCH FUN.

521
00:19:28,876 --> 00:19:32,088
THIS IS NOT FUN!

522
00:19:32,088 --> 00:19:33,339
ALL RIGHT, LOOK...

523
00:19:33,339 --> 00:19:35,133
ALL WE'RE TRYING
TO SAY IS

524
00:19:35,133 --> 00:19:37,468
DON'T LET WHAT
HAPPENED WITH CAROL

525
00:19:37,468 --> 00:19:39,595
RUIN WHAT YOU'VE
GOT WITH EMILY.

526
00:19:41,597 --> 00:19:43,808
THE '92 ROSS WOULDN'T.

527
00:19:45,101 --> 00:19:46,393
THANKS.

528
00:19:48,437 --> 00:19:50,023
STILL THINK I WAS RIGHT

529
00:19:50,023 --> 00:19:52,399
ABOUT THAT WHOLE MARK THING
THOUGH.

530
00:19:52,399 --> 00:19:54,485
WHA... YA... WHA...
YOU KNOW WHAT?

531
00:19:54,485 --> 00:19:56,112
I HOPE EMILY IS A LESBIAN.

532
00:19:59,157 --> 00:20:01,450
( drum rattling )

533
00:20:02,618 --> 00:20:03,911
DRUM ROLL.

534
00:20:05,038 --> 00:20:07,331
OKAY, OKAY...

535
00:20:07,331 --> 00:20:08,958
ALL RIGHT.

536
00:20:08,958 --> 00:20:10,208
HELP.

537
00:20:10,208 --> 00:20:14,088
AM I A MARK OR A JOHN?

538
00:20:14,088 --> 00:20:17,967
WELL, YOU'RE NOT TALL
ENOUGH TO BE A MARK...

539
00:20:17,967 --> 00:20:20,887
BUT YOU MIGHT MAKE
A GOOD BARNEY.

540
00:20:20,887 --> 00:20:22,722
ALL RIGHT, LOOK,
I'M SERIOUS, OKAY?

541
00:20:22,722 --> 00:20:24,057
TOMORROW AT 3:30

542
00:20:24,057 --> 00:20:25,933
I'M GOING DOWN
TO THE COURTHOUSE.

543
00:20:25,933 --> 00:20:27,768
YOU'LL ACTUALLY GO
THROUGH WITH THIS?

544
00:20:27,768 --> 00:20:31,189
HEY, LOOK, THIS NAME HAS BEEN
HOLDING ME BACK MY ENTIRE LIFE.

545
00:20:31,189 --> 00:20:32,857
OKAY, IT'S PROBABLY WHY KIDS
PICKED ON ME IN SCHOOL

546
00:20:32,857 --> 00:20:34,650
AND WHY I NEVER DO WELL
WITH WOMEN.

547
00:20:34,650 --> 00:20:36,736
SO, AS OF 4:00 TOMORROW,
I'M EITHER GOING TO BE

548
00:20:36,736 --> 00:20:38,571
MARK JOHNSON
OR JOHN MARKSON.

549
00:20:40,156 --> 00:20:41,699
YOU'VE GOT PROBLEMS
BECAUSE OF YOU,

550
00:20:41,699 --> 00:20:43,159
NOT YOUR NAME.

551
00:20:45,203 --> 00:20:46,954
ALL RIGHT, THIS
HAS GOT TO STOP.

552
00:20:46,954 --> 00:20:49,082
CHANDLER IS
A GREAT NAME.

553
00:20:49,082 --> 00:20:51,084
IN FACT...

554
00:20:51,084 --> 00:20:52,418
YES.

555
00:20:52,418 --> 00:20:53,586
I'M... I'M SORRY.

556
00:20:53,586 --> 00:20:55,379
I KNOW YOU
REALLY WANTED ME

557
00:20:55,379 --> 00:20:57,297
TO NAME THE BABY
JOEY, BUT...

558
00:20:57,297 --> 00:20:58,883
SO, I'M-I'M GOING TO...

559
00:20:58,883 --> 00:21:01,260
I'M GOING TO NAME
THE BABY CHANDLER.

560
00:21:03,846 --> 00:21:05,305
REALLY?

561
00:21:05,305 --> 00:21:07,558
YEAH, BUT YOU HAVE
TO KEEP THE NAME, TOO.

562
00:21:07,558 --> 00:21:08,559
OKAY.

563
00:21:08,559 --> 00:21:09,602
THANKS.
OKAY.

564
00:21:09,602 --> 00:21:10,853
YOU WANT TO HUG IT OUT?

565
00:21:10,853 --> 00:21:11,854
YEAH.

566
00:21:11,854 --> 00:21:12,855
YAY.

567
00:21:12,855 --> 00:21:13,856
YAY.

568
00:21:13,856 --> 00:21:15,357
YAY. OH, YAY!

569
00:21:15,357 --> 00:21:18,444
OKAY, I GOT TO GO TELL
FRANK AND ALICE RIGHT NOW.

570
00:21:18,444 --> 00:21:19,862
OOH.

571
00:21:19,862 --> 00:21:21,197
GOOD-BYE, PHEEBS.

572
00:21:21,197 --> 00:21:22,573
OKAY, BYE.

573
00:21:22,573 --> 00:21:24,283
( devious laughter )

574
00:21:24,283 --> 00:21:26,035
( horrified gasp )

575
00:21:38,589 --> 00:21:39,882
( both moaning )

576
00:21:43,261 --> 00:21:44,595
THAT'S NICE LUGGAGE.

577
00:21:44,595 --> 00:21:46,222
YEAH, I WAS
GOING TO SAY.

578
00:21:46,222 --> 00:21:48,224
HEY!

579
00:21:48,224 --> 00:21:49,809
HI!
HI!

580
00:21:49,809 --> 00:21:51,310
I MISSED YOU.

581
00:21:51,310 --> 00:21:53,729
OH, I MISSED
YOU, TOO.

582
00:21:53,729 --> 00:21:54,730
HEY, THANKS
FOR EVERYTHING.

583
00:21:54,730 --> 00:21:56,065
I HAD SUCH A GREAT TIME.

584
00:21:56,065 --> 00:21:57,357
OH, SO DID I.

585
00:21:58,776 --> 00:22:00,778
THERE'S NO TONGUE.

586
00:22:00,778 --> 00:22:02,238
( sighs )

